---
interface Props {
  caption?: boolean;
}

const { caption = true } = Astro.props;
---

<figure class="pigment-switch not-prose my-8">
  <svg viewBox="0 0 400 420" role="img" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
    <title>The melanocortin pigment switch</title>
    <desc>
      In human melanocytes, alpha-MSH activates MC1R and favors brown-black
      eumelanin over red-yellow pheomelanin. Eumelanin absorbs some ultraviolet
      radiation and helps protect DNA. In the lizard example, melanocortin
      signaling instead darkens skin rapidly by dispersing existing pigment
      within melanophores.
    </desc>

    <g text-anchor="middle">
      <text class="heading" x="200" y="37">Human melanocyte</text>

      <rect class="node" x="24" y="56" width="91" height="40" rx="8" />
      <text class="label" x="69.5" y="81">α-MSH</text>
      <path class="connector" d="M115 76 H144 m-5-5 5 5-5 5" />
      <rect class="node accent-node" x="152" y="56" width="96" height="40" rx="8" />
      <text class="label" x="200" y="81">MC1R</text>
      <path class="connector" d="M248 76 H277 m-5-5 5 5-5 5" />
      <rect class="node" x="285" y="56" width="91" height="40" rx="8" />
      <text class="label" x="330.5" y="81">Eumelanin</text>

      <text class="detail" x="200" y="121">MC1R activation favors eumelanin</text>
      <text class="detail" x="200" y="139">over red-yellow pheomelanin.</text>

      <path class="divider" d="M24 157 H376 M200 175 V402" />
      <text class="heading" x="105" y="186">Lizard skin</text>
      <text class="heading" x="295" y="186">Human skin</text>

      <!-- The same pigment is shown clustered and dispersed. -->
      <g class="cell">
        <circle cx="66" cy="258" r="26" />
        <circle cx="145" cy="258" r="26" />
      </g>
      <path class="connector" d="M96 258 H115 m-5-5 5 5-5 5" />
      <path class="particles" d="M61 254h0 M69 254h0 M65 261h0 M72 263h0 M59 262h0
        M134 247h0 M153 245h0 M145 257h0 M132 265h0 M157 269h0" />
      <text class="detail" x="66" y="307">Clustered</text>
      <text class="detail" x="145" y="307">Dispersed</text>

      <!-- A dashed continuation indicates that some UV can still pass. -->
      <text class="detail" x="295" y="216">UV</text>
      <path class="connector" d="M273 224 V250 M295 224 V250 M317 224 V250
        M269 245 l4 5 4-5 M291 245 l4 5 4-5 M313 245 l4 5 4-5" />
      <rect class="pigment-band" x="224" y="258" width="142" height="22" rx="5" />
      <text class="label" x="295" y="274">Eumelanin</text>
      <path class="connector residual" d="M295 283 V296" />
      <text class="detail" x="295" y="313">DNA</text>

      <text class="label" x="105" y="354">Pigment disperses</text>
      <text class="detail" x="105" y="375">Skin darkens in minutes.</text>
      <text class="label" x="295" y="354">Some UV is absorbed</text>
      <text class="detail" x="295" y="375">Less UV reaches DNA.</text>
    </g>
  </svg>

  {
    caption && (
      <figcaption>
        Melanocortin signaling changes pigmentation in two ways. In the lizard
        example, melanophores disperse pigment they already contain. In human
        melanocytes, α-MSH activates MC1R and shifts pigment production toward
        brown-black eumelanin, which absorbs some UV and helps protect DNA.
      </figcaption>
    )
  }
</figure>

<style>
  .pigment-switch {
    max-width: 34rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  svg {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 0.75rem;
    background: var(--bg-elevated);
    font-family: var(--font-sans, system-ui);
  }

  .heading {
    fill: var(--text);
    font-family: var(--font-serif, Georgia);
    font-size: 20px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .label,
  .detail {
    font-size: 15px;
  }

  .label {
    fill: var(--text);
    font-weight: 650;
  }

  .detail {
    fill: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .node,
  .cell,
  .pigment-band {
    fill: var(--bg-elevated);
    stroke: var(--border);
    stroke-width: 1.25;
  }

  .accent-node,
  .pigment-band {
    fill: var(--accent-soft);
    stroke: var(--accent);
  }

  .divider {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--border);
  }

  .connector,
  .particles {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--text-muted);
    stroke-linecap: round;
    stroke-linejoin: round;
    stroke-width: 1.75;
  }

  .particles {
    stroke: var(--accent);
    stroke-width: 5;
  }

  .residual {
    stroke-dasharray: 2 4;
  }

  figcaption {
    margin: 0.75rem auto 0;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    text-align: center;
  }
</style>
